## Building a Tip Calculator

### The Core Calculation

```xiom
fn calculate_tip(bill: Int, tip_percent: Int) -> Int {
  bill * tip_percent / 100
}

fn calculate_total(bill: Int, tip_percent: Int) -> Int {
  bill + calculate_tip(bill, tip_percent)
}

fn split_bill(bill: Int, tip_percent: Int, people: Int) -> Int {
  let total = calculate_total(bill, tip_percent);
  total / people
}
```

### Common Tip Percentages

```xiom
fn tip_breakdown(bill: Int, people: Int) {
  let pct_15 = calculate_tip(bill, 15);
  let pct_18 = calculate_tip(bill, 18);
  let pct_20 = calculate_tip(bill, 20);
  let pct_25 = calculate_tip(bill, 25);

  io.println(pct_15);
  io.println(pct_18);
  io.println(pct_20);
  io.println(pct_25);

  if people > 1 {
    io.println(split_bill(bill, 20, people));
  };
}
```

### Rounding

```xiom
fn round_up(amount: Int) -> Int {
  if amount % 10 >= 5 { return (amount / 10 + 1) * 10; };
  (amount / 10) * 10
}
```

### Example Usage

```
Bill: $87
Tip: 20% → $17
Total: $104
Per person (3): $34

Breakdown:
  15% → $13
  18% → $15
  20% → $17
  25% → $21
```

### Service Quality Guide

- Excellent: 20-25%
- Good: 15-20%
- Average: 10-15%
- Poor: 0-10% (consider not tipping but leaving feedback)

